The invention relates to a method (METH) for measuring a distance R between a vehicle (V) and an identifier (I) for accessing and starting the vehicle (V), the vehicle (V) and the identifier (I) being synchronized. The method (METH) comprises the following steps:

- selecting (Sel_fp) N frequencies fp, where p ∈ [1, N] and N is a natural number greater than 3;
- implementing N sequences Sqp, each sequence Sqp comprising the following steps:
  - transmitting (Em_Svp) a first signal (Svp), having a frequency fp, from a transmitter (TXv) of the vehicle (V) to a receiver (RXi) of the identifier (I);
  - measuring (Mes_φvip), using a calculator (Xi) of the identifier (I), a phase φvip, modulo 2π, of the received first signal (Svp) relative to a second signal (Sip) having a phase φip(t) = φ0ip + 2πfpt;
  - transmitting (Em_Sip) the second signal (Sip) from a transmitter (TXi) of the identifier (I) to a receiver (RXv) of the vehicle (V);
  - measuring (Mes_φivp), using a calculator (Xv) of the vehicle (V), a phase φivp, modulo 2π, of the received second signal (Sip) relative to the first signal (Svp); and
  - calculating (Cal_φp) the average φp of the phases φvip and φivp;
- for each p from 1 to N − 1, calculating (Cal_Pp) a ramp Pp according to the formula:

  Pp = (φp+1 − φp)/(fp+1 − fp); and

- calculating (Cal_R) the distance R from the ramps Pp, where p ∈ [1, N].

