The invention concerns a process (METH) for determining the distance \(R\) separating a vehicle \(V\) from an identifier \(I\) used to unlock and start the vehicle, with the vehicle \(V\) and identifier \(I\) synchronized. The process includes:

- choosing (Sel_fp) \(N\) frequencies \(f_p\), where \(p \in [1,N]\) and \(N\) is a natural number greater than 3;
- carrying out \(N\) sequences \(S_{qp}\), each of which includes:
  - using a vehicle transmitter \(TX_v\) to send (Em_Svp) a first signal \(S_{vp}\), at frequency \(f_p\), to a receiver \(RX_i\) in the identifier \(I\);
  - employing a calculator \(X_i\) in the identifier to measure (Mes_φvip), modulo \(2\pi\), the phase \(\varphi_{vip}\) of the received first signal \(S_{vp}\) relative to a second signal \(S_{ip}\), whose phase is defined by  
    \[
    \varphi_{ip}(t)=\varphi_{0ip}+2\pi f_p t;
    \]
  - transmitting (Em_Sip) the second signal \(S_{ip}\) from an identifier transmitter \(TX_i\) to a vehicle receiver \(RX_v\);
  - using a vehicle calculator \(X_v\) to determine (Mes_φivp), modulo \(2\pi\), the phase \(\varphi_{ivp}\) of the received second signal \(S_{ip}\) relative to the first signal \(S_{vp}\);
  - computing (Cal_φp) the mean phase \(\varphi_p\) from phases \(\varphi_{vip}\) and \(\varphi_{ivp}\);
- for every \(p\) from 1 through \(N-1\), deriving (Cal_Pp) a slope \(P_p\) according to  
  \[
  P_p=\frac{\varphi_{p+1}-\varphi_p}{f_{p+1}-f_p};
  \]
- and determining (Cal_R) the distance \(R\) from the slopes \(P_p\), with \(p \in [1,N]\).

