1. **A method for determining a distance between a vehicle and an electronic key, the method comprising:**

selecting at least four carrier frequencies;

for each selected carrier frequency, exchanging a ranging signal between a vehicle transceiver of the vehicle and a key transceiver of the electronic key in a vehicle-to-key direction and a key-to-vehicle direction;

measuring, at each selected carrier frequency, a first phase associated with the ranging signal received by the key transceiver and a second phase associated with the ranging signal received by the vehicle transceiver;

calculating, for each selected carrier frequency, an averaged bidirectional phase based on the first phase and the second phase;

computing, from the averaged bidirectional phases, a plurality of phase-versus-frequency ramps, each phase-versus-frequency ramp representing a change in averaged bidirectional phase over a frequency interval between respective selected carrier frequencies; and

deriving the distance between the vehicle and the electronic key based on the plurality of phase-versus-frequency ramps.
